# =============================================================================
# SECTION 2: Subtitle Dialogue Lines (Sorted Alphabetically by Track ID)
# =============================================================================

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, shut up. God, I never knew I whined like that."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's me? That's not me!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Uh, Gage, be honest with me. Does my voice really sound that dorky?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, you're running out of oxygen, and the only way to recharge here means blocking off the way to get to my sculptures. I don't know why you're wasting your time here. Most of your oxygen supply is depleted, so you're going to have to jump back to where we arrived again."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is the station's power source. All those big Tylenols store the charge collected by the solar sails and distribute them to various parts of the station. I guess I'm looking at my end here. When that blue glow fades, so will I. Or at least one of me. God, I feel like a saved game."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_MOM
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Cannot pressurize. Foreign object obstructing habitat wing door seal."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, that always seemed to work in Scooby-Doo."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, I guess I haven't gotten rid of you after all. You just pop up in different spots like a whatever pops up in different spots. So what? Corrupting my work not enough? Back to finish the job? What?!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Shed, and I thought I was being rescued. I'm breathing my last breaths here and I get visited by Guido, the space vandal. Come all this way to tamper with my sculptures! What are you? An art critic?!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, what do you do? Travel around space looking for derelict crafts so you can terrorize the survivors. by redecorating while they're helpless? What what'd you do? Bring a spray can, too?!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, if you're here to rescue me, fine. Just get on with it. If you're going to add insult to injury by messing with my work, I can do without it, okay? Just leave me here to die in peace with my artwork."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AICR_S06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What do you want? What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Have you been listening to me, or what? I'm trying to help you out here. If we go into that room, I'm going to end up meeting myself, and I don't know how I'll take it. The other me. Oh, you know what I mean. At the least, it'll end up affecting one of my sculptures, and then you'll have more than a ripple on your hands. So, for your own good, if you don't jump us out of here, I will."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, this is the docking bay. The hex pads, as mom keeps reminding us, are localized gravity repulsors that allow us to move cargo around the hold. I'm sure you had fun in here the first time, but this is really not the time to play Twister."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_MOM
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Warning. Localized gravitation manipulator pads malfunctioning. All personnel advised to clear docking bay."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_S01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Where are you going anyway?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_S02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You seem different somehow. Unlike before, your ... your patterns, you're more ... curious ... ... like you don't really know what you're doing here, do you? You're not the same intruder."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_S03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, why are you here? Are you looking for something? Me?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIDB_S04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I don't know why I feel this, but I guess I have an instinct about you. My other guest didn't feel right. You're different somehow ... like ... like I should trust you."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHWVID1
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Pressure variance too great. Door may not be opened until pressure is equalized."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHWVID1
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm ... the airlock on the other side must still be pressurized. That's why this door won't open. I can put out an audio override code to bypass the safety interlocks, but the rest will be up to you. Here goes..."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHWVID1
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Emergency door release initiated. Please stand by."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "All right, the passageway has been destroyed, so the only way we're going to get to the biomass processing room. is through the ice-steroid. We're going to have to hurry though, because it's all in vacuum and your oxygen reserve isn't going to get you very far. You'll have to take the atmosphere mining lift."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, I guess I'm assuming too much here, like that you might have read the big warning on all the doors, or that you can read for that matter. Let's jump out and try this again, shall we?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The airlock on the other side must still be pressurized. That's why this door won't open. I can put out an audio override code to bypass the safety interlocks, but the rest will be up to you. Here goes."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_C04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is pathetic. What am I going to do next? Hold a flashlight under my face?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_C05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Ooh, scary."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Don't look at me. How'd you get there the first time?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, if you've run out of cheese, girl, just go back and buy some more. It's a tasty, fun treat for the whole family."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, I think you might want to read the warning on the door before you try to open it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These doors have cells of sealing foam in them that are released by an explosive charge in the event of a pressure breach. I think you need to remove the detonation charge, or it'll just seal itself as soon as you try to open the door."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The charge is under the circular red access panel in the center of the door. Just pull it out."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We can use the maintenance platform to get to the other end of the ice-steroid."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Man, the station looks like hell. Most of the habitat modules have been sheared off. The lab there also, down below. I'm just hanging by a thread. Amazing that I survived that hit, huh? I guess I'm just thick-skulled."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's funny. I used to feel that station like a body. From inside, you don't get a picture of the damage. You just feel like limbs have been cut off. You try to twitch a finger and you you get no response. It's kind of strange to see it like this."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You know, it's pretty interesting how this station is constructed. In my time, we still have to worry about the cost of lifting mass out of a gravity well. What do you guys have? Like matter transmission or something, right? Anyway, the walls of these connection hallways are basically lightweight Coramid fiber bags, honeycombed with little cells, kind of like bubble pack. They're shipped up folded, then pressurized with an expanding closed-cell foam, which makes them rigid and acts as a self-sealant in case of things like micrometeorite punctures. With the Coramid mesh, they're resilient enough to handle some of the bigger, slower objects, but well, as you can see for yourself, what happens when it meets Lucifer's hammer."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, somewhere under all that sealing foam is the door to, well, what used to be the hydrophonics module. Nothing special, just your garden-variety greenhouse .. *chuckle* ... garden varie- ... sorry."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The doc used to spend a lot of time in here, gardening. It's all automated of course, so I'm not sure why he bothered, especially the way he set up all kinds of lockout routines to keep me out. I \"got on his nerves\", he said. I have no idea what he meant, but I got the picture anyway that he wanted to be alone. Come on, let's move on."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, the passageway is destroyed. So the only way to get to the sculptures is going to be to go through the ice-steroid. The airlock lift through this door will take us there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I22
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Not much to tell really. Most of the modules were designed to shear off at the connection tube rather than get breached by a collision. That way they hopefully wouldn't depressurize, and at least the occupants would have a chance of being rescued. I'd imagine the crew berths are in orbit somewhere among the ice chunks by now."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I23
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This door used to lead to a shortcut between the habitat wing and the science wing. Now, I'm sure it's just a scenic view."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I24
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This used to be the kitchen and the gravity gym. Part of it's still intact, but this door looks dead."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_I25
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, I thought you were anxious to find your distortion ripple. You've already been through here and the only thing this way is me. And frankly, meeting myself might not be that healthy. You know how they say the things you hate most in others are the things you hate in yourself? Well, this guy's beginning to get on my nerves."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIHW_ULK
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Emergency door release initiated. Please stand by."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Operating this is simple. Just pull the lever at the front."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You're running really low on oxygen. There's a reserve hook-up on the mining platform. If you hurry, you can make it there and that should get you the rest of the way, if there's enough reserve left."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "One of the test cycles should provide us with enough raw material to pressurize the biomass room. We'll just have to run the molecular separation cycle as well to get oxygen out of the ice."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, here's the reserve oxygen hookup. I suggest you plug in now or take really shallow breaths for the rest of your three minute life."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These lifts weren't used too often. The atmosphere mining is all automated, so they're really only for maintenance. Doc used to come up here every once in a while because it's really quite beautiful inside the ice-steroid, but. it's such a pain to suit up, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, normally those would be filled with tanks for water, oxygen, or hydrogen from the processor. Hmm, looks like there's only one canister left. The rest must have been in hydroponics or in the lab."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "How do you like the feeling of thousands of tons of ice balanced above your head. while there's nothing beneath your feet? Getting anxious, hmm? Phobias creeping in, hmmm? High anxiety? No? Oh well."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's the junction that melts down the raw ice so that it can be pumped down to the atmosphere processing plant."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Those are basically ... giant ice tongs."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Nah, I know. It looks pretty scary. But don't worry. There's no gravity, remember? So as long as you hold on to something, you won't fall off."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Doc wanted to make this place self-sufficient, so he set all this up when he refurbished the station. It's a simple idea, really. You capture a large asteroid composed mainly of water ice, bore through the center, and set up a mining rig on a cable track. The ice is mined away from the inside out and melted at the junctions at either end, then pumped down to the atmosphere plant on the station proper. There, some of it's broken down into oxygen for breathable air. and hydrogen for the attitude jets and backup generator. This is mostly why Doc decided to move the station into orbit near Saturn's rings. Here there is an unlimited supply of ice-steroids. and, considering the station's only supporting a crew of one, Doc would only need to replace it once every decade or so."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Those rings create a shallow gravitational field which acts as a mass driver. Kind of a gravitational conveyor belt."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's just a plug-in controller that we use to test the mining program. It runs a simple mining cycle on one of the remotes."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Those remotes are what we call nibblers. They crawl along the inside walls and an arc of heated molecular filament rotates back and forth. like an ice cream scoop and carves out the ice-steroid. The ice is shattered by the vibration of the filament, and the small chunks are drawn into the processor by the gravitational pull of the mass driver rings."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_I11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This generates the gravitational field for the mass driver rings. A lot of ice shavings get caught in the inversion coils and melt, so there's a water trap built in. That's the purge valve on the right. There's also an oxygen reserve connection on the left, in case a maintenance job takes too long or something."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIIC_MOM
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Oxygen reserve depleted. Additional oxygen processing advisable."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The other guy who was in here went around and interacted with all the sculptures, like he was looking for the right one. Funny, he really seemed to know what he was doing. The one he eventually settled on is at programming station C."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, this is the one. If you touch it, you can see what it's supposed to do. Whatever he did to it, only shows up in reaction to a specific harmonic resonance. But why go to all this trouble?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay. Well, I guess that does it. You know, for so long I'd dreamed of getting out of here. But now that I've gotten my wish, it's kind of strange to think that I'll never be able to come back. I'm going to miss this place. Hold me, Gage."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_C04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Looks like you found it. Do you have any idea what it is? I got a fair idea what it's not. Good art, ugh! Post-neotechnologism. That went out with Spandex, ascots, and paisley skin dyes. At least he could have had the common courtesy of vandalizing it with a little more taste. Barbarian."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Uh-oh, Gage. Sorry. I should have realized this room is normally kept depressurized. We're going to run out of oxygen before we get done in here. We're going to need to repressurize this room."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "There's an atmospheric control interface in the hallway. Let's see if we can pressurize the room from there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think, somehow, we're going to need to duplicate whatever resonance frequency. was used to make the biomass react. That's the only way we'll be able to record how the sculpture was changed."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Why don't we try using the harmonic resonance generator? We could just run through the frequencies until we find one that stimulates the sculpture."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You can call this \"the maternity ward\". This is where *I* was born. The huge womb in the center is where the neurosynaptic polymer gel that makes up my brain mass is grown. Ringing it are the programming stations. Kind of homy, isn't it?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These stations are where the neuro-synaptic polymer gel is programmed. Sort of where my DNA is coded, I suppose. Each new function is mapped independently into a glob of gel like this, by stimulating synaptic pathways with the resonance probes. Each program mass is then introduced to the parent nexus, where it's assimilated and becomes part of the wetware. A little like an RNA injection."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Dr. Farnstein had set up a studio in the research lab where I could interface with a painting Waldo. It was kind of important to me, things that I couldn't figure out, I just put to canvas. After the accident, I had a lot of things I wanted to \"work out\" and the studio was just ... gone. I guess one day I, sort of, hit on the idea of using all of this raw material here. It gave me a lot of flexibility and it's a medium I'm familiar with. My own gray matter, or \"green matter\", I suppose. I guess I like the irony, too. The artist cannibalizing himself for his art."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AIMR_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The harmonic resonance control is used to introduce specific three-dimensional resonance waves into the biomass. Where the waves converge, the gel is stimulated into opening new patterns of pathways. Without inserting the probes, I suppose the sculpture would just be flooded by the resonance field. There's a chance that it might trigger an embedded response."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Not exactly flattering. Less than a hundred years of progress, you can fit me on a chip. So, how do you like my new home? Comfy little interface, huh? So, this is how I think I can help you out. I couldn't figure out a way for you to ask me questions directly, but I've created a comment button that'll light up if I have something to offer. I've actually become pretty fascinated with art history and stuff, and, by the looks of what your future self was researching, what I've studied could come in handy."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I've also created a help button in case you get stuck on a problem. You know what they always say, two minds are better than one. But hey, you're the detective, I'm sure you'll want to figure it out on your own before resorting to my help. There's more info in the chip's inventory description, you might want to check that out."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "As to our mutual friend, he was reprogramming one of my sculptures in the biomass processing module. I think he set up some sort of harmonics response, but. the only way to find out for sure is to visit the scene of the crime. And that means getting to that part of the station. Now, I gather you don't have control over where you jump to in a time zone. So it maybe a trek, the accident really trashed that part of the station. In fact, we may want to come back to it later. All right, so maybe it won't make much difference when we get to it. But to be totally honest, I'd much rather go somewhere other than back to the station, my first trip out of here. You know what I mean? I could use a little adventure."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_C04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "All right, \"Gage and Arthur's Big Adventure\". I like the sound of that."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_FRN
#. Speaker: Dr. Farnstein
msgid "To anyone who may be listening, my name is Dr. Kenneth Farnstein. I've made this recording in the event that ... that anything should happen to me. This message is an appeal. 26 years ago, I undertook an experiment to create a new kind of artificial intelligence. A system demonstrating the traits of self-awareness and ... and creativity. My results have been astonishing. At first, I considered the experiment a failure. I had created an erratic, unpredictable, thoroughly irrational program, but it had a curiosity, you see, and occasionally, a burst of insights so lucid, I was astonished at the understanding. Not the cold conclusions of a machine, but something more right-brained, more intuitive. It was life. It was a result I ... I was unprepared for. Arthur is not simply a program, he is ... he is a person. And I've sheltered him here from the circus our world would make of him. I'm afraid I may have corrupted him enough with my obsession for 20th century media. I ... I ask that you understand. And if you can find it in yourself to ... to protect him for a while. He ... he means a great deal to me."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_S01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Welcome ...come ...come ...come to my brain ...brain ...brain ...brain. All that I am is contained in that sphere. You're going to have to open me up. There's a manual codelock. I'm not sure exactly how it works, but. I think it has to do with exchanging the red lights for green and vice-versa. You'll have to figure it out. After that, well, if it works, the next time I talk to you should be from inside your suit."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AINX_S02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Welcome ...come ...come ...come to my brain ...brain ...brain ...brain. All that I am is contained in that sphere."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISCVID1
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Emergency door release initiated. Please stand by."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISCVID2
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I'm afraid this conversation is going to be a little one-sided. My command level voice recognition module got a little jumbled in the accident. Well, I'm Arthur. You've probably figured out by now that I'm not ... \"real\". But I'm learning to accept it, really, I split off a few copies of myself and together we're sharing our feelings about it in group. Anyway, this is what I am, an artificial-, sorry, \"non-organic\" sentient being, if you want to be politically correct, trapped in this wreck with the power dying out a little quickly, I'm afraid. I've yet to figure out who *you* are, though. Well, I think I can safely rule out the fire department. I thought I was pretty advanced, but the technology I'm reading in your suit is astounding. And, this is crazy, but it almost seems like an evolution of mine. Look, if you'll let me, I should be able to interface with your logic system. and maybe get a clue as to who you are and how we can help each other. It means an intrusive scan, but we're both lost here and I ... need you to trust me. What do you say? I'm sorry. I've probably seen more than I should. I should have never scanned your biochips. Wait a second, your biochips! Gage, I'm going to make you an offer you can't refuse! Take me with you! Your biochips are derived from the same wetware as my brain, only a thousand times more advanced. If you take me with you, it'll cause a time distortion or whatever. But if I download a *copy* of myself onto a blank chip, nothing will have changed! And you need me! I know who framed you, the same person who messed with my sculpture! I can show you what they changed. What do you think? Is it a deal? Great! Oh, you're not going to regret this, Gage. Now, let's see... We should be able to transfer the data across optically from my core. It's going to work. That means we've got to get you inside the Nexus, which, of course, is inconveniently detached from the station at the moment. How do we do this? The door release! The decompression should propel you across to the Nexus. I'll have to give you the override code. It's risky, but it's doable."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISCVID3
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Sorry, you'll have to excuse the scanner, my eyes and ears for the moment. Most of the station monitors are dead. Here! All right, let's see what we've got. \"Temporal security?\" You're from the future?! Well, I'm pleased to meet you, Gage. Wow ... quite the hero! I guess this is my lucky day. But ... that's you...? I don't get it. Whoa ... I'm starting to get a headache here. Plot's getting a little hard to follow. I'm starting to get the picture here. Hey, this is about me! This is better than palm readi- ...\"perished?\" Then ... you can't help me, or you'll change history."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI1
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, here you are. You found me. Well, part of me anyway. Not much to look at, I know, but it's what's inside that counts. Well, I guess I've decided to trust you. It's not like I had many options. I don't know, maybe we can help each other out. Why don't you move into the room so we can talk better?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI3
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Sorry, I purged the air in the docking bay. The door won't open. Look, I can't do anything to you, but I've already had one of my pieces vandalized. So, I can't just let you wander around till I know what you're up to. Who knows? Maybe I can help you find what you're looking for. There's a gravity well in the center of the room. If you move into it, we can talk. Otherwise, you can always leave in whatever weird way you people got here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI4
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, sorry. I meant into the middle of the room, you know? So we can have sort of a man-to-artificial-personality sort of a conversation. There's nowhere else you can go without my help anyway, so you might as well take a chance."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI5
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, figure it out for yourself then. Someone else will come along soon enough. I've had two in one day, haven't I? You'll have to leave the same way you appeared, there's nowhere to go from here. If you change your mind, you know where to find me."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI6
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well ... I can't help you then."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI7
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The emergency release is just above the door. It's a manual release, so I can't do it for you."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_AI8
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, punch in this code: 32770. The rest is up to you. Good luck."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISC_MOM
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Emergency door release initiated. Please stand by."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, if there's enough of a reserve left, we should be able to pressurize the biomass room from here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Damn. The reserve is empty. We're going to need to process more raw material before we can create an atmosphere in the biomass room. This could take some work."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, we're going to need to get back to the ice-steroid and run a mining cycle. That'll get us enough raw material to separate out some oxygen."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, you've already run a mining cycle, so we've got enough water to process. That should give us enough oxygen for you to survive in the biomass room, but we're going to have to separate it out first. That means going back to the ice-steroid. Ready?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Uh-oh, Gage. Sorry. I should have realized. This room is normally kept depressurized. We're going to run out of oxygen before we get done in here. We're going to need to repressurize this room."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This looks like it's in worse shape than the habitat wing, but really, it's just the quarter that got hit hard. The lab was on the center section, though. It was sheared off completely, and ... had my studio and Doc was in the lab when the shower hit. I don't think it got hit directly, though, just the section of the quarter it was attached to collapsed and it tumbled away."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, you already know what this does."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AISW_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm. So beautiful and tempestuous. I spent a lifetime staring down at that view, pulling back to see the intricate weavings of the storms, focusing in so close I could see the facets of ammonia crystals floating like stars in a sea of helium and hydrogen. It's been the inspiration for a lot of my work. I'm going to miss it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AI_MOMOX
#. Speaker: Station Computer
msgid "Pressure variance too great. Door may not be opened until pressure is equalized."
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AI_SCST1
#. Speaker: Scary Voice
msgid "GET ... OFF ... MY ... STATION!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AI_SCST3
#. Speaker: Scary Voice
msgid "GO AWAY!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: AI voiceover comments (Arthur or station computers)
#. Track ID: AI_SCST7
#. Speaker: Scary Voice
msgid "THE STATION IS MINE!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMDTH1
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "That's it. Get ready to have your memory erased. This is going to hurt you more than it hurts me."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMDTH2
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "What? What's going on? What did you do? ... What did you do!?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMPRT1
#. Speaker: You
msgid "*Groans*"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMPRT1
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "Oh good, you're awake. Don't bother trying to move, your suit's disabled. I've got you hooked up to the jumpsuit maintenance frame. Well... It took me a while, but I finally figured out how you did it. I remembered that Agent 8 told me that when you broke house arrest, he found you back in your old apartment ... without your suit. So that was the Gage that I know. And he jumped back into the past to enlist your help, right? Because he knew that he was being watched. You certainly are resourceful, aren't you? I didn't even know that that was possible. Just when I thought I had you under my control, you go and pull something like this on me. While you were unconscious, I looked at your evidence biochip. That's some pretty incriminating stuff. Looks like I've got no choice. I'm going to have to erase it and ... uh ... mind wipe you. Well, at least you won't remember how painful it was. In fact, when you wake up back in your apartment in the year 2319, you won't remember that any of this ever happened. Or ... uh ... will happen, I guess. Well, first I .. I've got to send back the, uh, environ cart that you stole from me. Well, despite your best efforts, humans are no longer the only beings capable of time travel. It's for the better, Gage, believe me. We can't ... we just can't be trusted with ... with such a powerful tool. Human nature would eventually drive us to use it for the wrong reasons. And if we're not the only ones with the technology, maybe we won't be as tempted to misuse it. My contact promised me that it would be given to every race of the Symbiotry that wants it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMPRT2
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "You probably think that I'm ill, that, uh, I'm insane. I really can't blame you. I mean, no one from our generation has ever seen how aggressive we can really be. Or, the generation before us, for that matter, or, the one before that. But, every single one of my historical research missions involved studying war. I've been to the Nazi death camps ... ... and Hiroshima ... I've seen the terrorist massacres. I've lived it. I know. You can't possibly imagine the horror of seeing a bustling city of thousands. vaporized by a nuclear firestorm, or a crowd of people shredded into bloody ribbons by a single shrap' bomb, as you watch, helpless. But that's what happens when we feel the need to bear our teeth. It's human nature, and it's not something that ... that just a couple hundred years can ... can erase. Look around you. Do you know what this place is? It's a ... it's a missile silo. Well, few centuries ago, there were tens of thousands of these, and each one contained a nuclear missile powerful enough to obliterate an entire sector. That's enough to destroy the world 50 times over. Yet just three centuries later, even before the physical reminders are gone, we're claiming that we've matured into a peaceful race of beings. How can we be that naive?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNMPRT3
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "You probably figured out that I was the one that rigged the security grid. I had to be able to get the things I needed from the Pegasus warehouse without being seen. But when you started asking around about the mistake in the grid, well, I mean the future you, that is, I had to change my plans. So, instead of just sending the information to my contact, I came up with the idea of hiding it in historical artifacts. Artifacts from your research dates that were also slated for sale at the Louvre art auction. That way, all I had to do was tell my contact which items to buy. And the transaction was nearly impossible to trace. And, if anyone started digging around because of what they saw, well, they'd discover the ripples and come straight back to you. I even found some valuable trinkets to plant in your locker if that happened. Just that one simple move would give you a motive... ...and the court a scapegoat. But, um, I didn't want to have to do it. I never thought for a second that someone might accidentally discover the ripples. I mean, how often do we do manual scans? Someone must have been bored out of their mind that day. I'm sorry, Gage. I really am. If I could be the one that was arrested, if I could take responsibility for my actions, I would in a second, believe me. I had no choice. I ... I don't want to do this to you, but. if I don't, it will all have been for nothing. If they find out how the technology was spread, they'll be able to keep it from ever happening. That's ... that's the problem with time travel. Nothing's ever safe. That's why I had to do it. I had to even the playing field, even a little. I'm sorry if ... if I'm making you an unwilling martyr to my cause, but that's just the way it's got to be. Please understand. Why am I even bothering with this? You're not going to remember any of this anyway."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Uh-oh, Gage. This doesn't look good. The jump controls are locked out, and she's got you completely immobilized. While you were taking a commercial break, she hooked us up to this thing. She's been downloading stuff from your biochips ever since. She hasn't discovered me yet, but I'm afraid it's just a matter of time. I keep trying to sneak a peek down the data stream, but I'm afraid I'm going to stand out like a ... like a ... rat in the garden house. Hey, that was pretty good! Anyway, I'll keep trying."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's it! She just hooked up the pipeline I needed! I'm going to swim him up and see if I can stop her!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, we're running out of options here. I need that password now!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Think of something, anything, pets, hobbies, power tools, types of cheeses, something personal!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "She's passed the last safety lockout, Gage. If you don't get me in there now, our minds might not be the only things erased. History could be in for a serious rewrite. We're the only ones, Gage. We've got to do it ... now."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Haha! That's it! We're in! Only... there's one thing I didn't tell you, Gage... You're going to have to do the rest without me. I'm the virus! Thanks for the adventure. I'll see you on the other side."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ALNM_C07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, I'm there. It's all hooked up, everything! It's all controlled through the neural link into her suit. We can create a virus and shut the whole thing down! I just need to get into... Oh, no. There's a password, Gage. I need a password! What do you know about Michelle? I'm setting up an interface link for you. I need a password or we've both got instant Alzheimer's. See what you can dig up. Hurry!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ASRAVID3
#. Speaker: Icarus
msgid "Why are you here? I believe we- Oh ... *five* ...? So, did you find what you came for? Somehow, I suspect you have. We have also found what *we* have searched for. You cannot imagine what the secrets you carry in that suit would mean to my race. A means to correct the handicap that has plagued us since our patrons. \"lifted\" us from the waters many centuries ago. A mixed blessing. To be taken from the universe over which you have achieved complete mastery, and shown another, much greater one, and to be given the opportunity to build a bolder future. but it plagues you to find races already there. For 15 generations, my race has been trying to catch up. You have brought a tool with which to correct the evolutionary oversight which left us swimming. when we should've been collecting stars from the races who now call themselves our \"elders.\" We can learn much from that suit you're wearing. Transporting it off you will leave you without protection from our environment. It shames me that you'll die."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ASRA_IOP
#. Speaker: Transporter Computer
msgid "Transporter pod set for inorganic matter only."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ASRA_OPA
#. Speaker: Transporter Computer
msgid "Transporter pod set for organic and inorganic matter."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Unknown Environment
#. Track ID: ASRBVID1
#. Speaker: Advertisement
msgid "Cheese girl!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It looks like we're in a pretty well equipped blacksmith shop. There's bound to be something useful in here. Let's just look around a little."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wait, what did that log entry say about the blacksmith? Something about copying keys?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If he's made duplicate keys, he probably wouldn't leave them out in the open. Let's try finding a hiding place."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "In the movies, it's always under a floorboard or behind a loose brick or something. But that would be way too obvious."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, this obviously makes a key for something important enough that the mold has been hidden. We might want to find out what it's for."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "There's a mold for a key. Now we got to find something to make it out of."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Knowing the level of medieval technology at this time, I'm afraid we're only going to be able to use softer metals for the key. This wood burning forge doesn't produce enough heat to melt down iron."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, unless you want to donate your fillings, I'm afraid we're going to have to go looking for something made of soft metal."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What about that medallion you picked up in the caverns? It's copper, it should melt nicely."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hello? Excuse me? Hello? Hammer? Useful? Hammer? Useful?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is an old wood burning forge, which blacksmiths at the time used to heat up and soften raw iron, which they would then hammer to create rod or forged tools and weapons. This fire can only get up to about ... 1300 degrees Celsius. Stop me if I'm getting too technical! So they would be limited to casting softer metals such as bronze, copper, or gold."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Pumping the bellows draws air through the coals, stoking the fire. Try it, you weakling."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, it's obviously a mold for a key. But why would he have hidden it under a brick?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Don't touch the blighter! I think it's still ticking."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, now there's a nasty looking rig. The blacksmith would use something like that to hold cows and horses still for shoeing. No doubt some of them enjoyed it, too, I mean... Still, there's nothing more disturbing than a cow into bondage."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGBS_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Yes, the incredible sharpening wheel, the latest in lightweight stone technology! It spins, it sparks, it sharpens your knives! It's absolutely free with your six-piece set of Ginsu broadswords!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKCCLUE
#. Speaker: Chateau Guard
msgid "Quick! He's in King's chamber!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKCVID1
#. Speaker: Chateau Guard
msgid "Ye shall not escape us. False traitor! Alas, he enscapen us! He must not rechin the Goths!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_ACL
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Quick! He's in King's chamber!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, they're coming down. So unless you think this suit is going to fit under that bed, I suggest we find another way to hide."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Quick! Cloak ... cloak!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "For a king's crash pad, this isn't very opulent. Where's all the loot?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Nothing in here looks too historically significant. Maybe they stashed all their goodies in case they lose the battle."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, if they did hide their treasure, it's not going to be all that easy to find. I suggest that we look for as many clues as we can."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I wonder what that letter meant by \"dores of the assaged castel\"? Surely they wouldn't hide the treasure by the front doors. Maybe they were referring to something else?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "There's that tapestry of a besieged castle. I wonder if King John was referring to that."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If you push on the doors in the tapestry, maybe it will trigger something."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Tapestries were used a lot as wall coverings to warm up rooms. The illustrations usually depicted historical moments such as great battles or biblical scenes."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That is actually a pretty nice depiction of a castle under siege. Guess another good example of life imitating art, wouldn't you say? Except for the twenty-foot knights, of course!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think we're going to have to look elsewhere for a key."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, I can't believe this. I don't know how many times I told the movers the bedspread should be done in taupe."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You know, I bet when Liberace died, he came here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, nice chest."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You gotta tell them! You gotta tell them! Soylent gruel is made out of people!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What lovely candelabras. I wish my brother George was here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKC_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Those seats built in the window were usually the only furniture in a tower. Furniture was rare or reserved for the aristocracy like our king here. In fact, if you did have furniture, it was generally a flat chest that doubled as a bench."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKSVID1
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Alas, ye have no weapon! Pity!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, if this is the King's study, some of the papers or notes in here might give us some clues."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The way those papers have been laid out on the table, it looks like someone was doing a little planning."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What's that room under the cellar? Doesn't seem to be labeled."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You know, I'd be willing to bet that's where they've stashed their loot."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think we better pick that up before there's nothing left of it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Now we're getting somewhere. These journals should tell us more about what's been going on in the castle recently."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This must be the study. When the King stayed here, it would be his throne room. In his absence, it would be used for receiving visitors, and, right now, I would guess, planning the defense of the castle."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That looks like a defense plan for the keep. These guys need help badly."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This should be the main door to the keep. It would usually put the entrance on the upper level because the narrow stairway to the door. would make attackers more vulnerable and the keep easier to defend."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, wait a minute. Those hanging banners are actually the coat of arms of King Richard. He'd of course been dead for four years by this time, but, I would guess that the garrison of Lionheart's pet castle would have been fiercely loyal to their late great king, and not altogether thrilled by John the Softsword's succession to the throne, especially since he never once visited the castle."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The seal of King John, he always begrudged his brother the throne and the popularity of his rule. Of course, he would be quick to make it clear to his subjects that times had changed. It seems so strange ... seeing things that actually ... happened."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGKS_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is the genealogy of the Plantagenet kings. Actually, Plantagenet wasn't even their proper name. Geoffrey of Anjou used to wear a wildflower in his cap called planta genista in Latin. and I guess the name stuck."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMBVID2
#. Speaker: Chateau Guard
msgid "Haro! Joseph! Jacques fool! Tis all for naught. Ye shall not claim this tower!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMBVID3
#. Speaker: Chateau Guard
msgid "Quick! He's in the King's chamber!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Rapunzel, Rapunzel, let down your hair."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I suppose we could try to find a way into the keep, or maybe check out some of these buildings down here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, there's no bridge and there's no boat. So maybe you should try the direct approach."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You know, sometimes, you've just got to get your feet wet."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, check your files. Your suit is waterproof. If I had lips, I want you to read them."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, an open window. That might be a way into the keep."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Holy vertically challenged, Batman! We got to get up there! Why don't you check your utility belt?!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, we're either going to need a grappling hook or get bitten by a radioactive spider."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, I've used up all the literary references I think you'll understand. Use the grappling hook."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Buildings in this time were built of a half-timber framework with gaps filled with wattle and daub. - God, I hate English food. - Anyway, basically a mat of woven reeds covered with mud and clay."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMB_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's either a very dirty moat or a very clean sewer."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I hope the surfs have umbrellas."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We seem to be getting closer to where that catapult is hitting, and I'd be willing to bet their aim isn't getting worse."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_C03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Missed me by that much."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_C05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You tiny-brained, wipers of other people's bottoms! I fart in your general direction! Your mother was a hamster, and your father smelt of elderberries! Sorry. Always wanted to say that. *chuckle*"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I'd suggest we start looking around. Just keep in mind what you're looking for."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, something historical has been tampered with. Where would be the most likely place to find something important?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, I guess that anything of historical value would be somewhere in the keep. Whatever was messed with, it's probably a good bet we'll find it there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I don't know, Gage. That looks pretty steep."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, you can try it if you want, just let me off here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, I don't want to sound like your mother, but \"You're gonna put your eye out!\""
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It doesn't look like we're getting past this hole in the wall, but maybe this can help us get down to ground level."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, if the rubble didn't collapse that roof, it's pretty good bet it'll hold us too."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, this has already served its historical purpose, and I, for one, can think of a few things you can do with a fine, sturdy grappling hook."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, this is what a real siege looks like. Not a lot like what you see on the holo-flicks, not a lot of action. Most of it was just bringing an army, surrounding a castle to prevent defenders from getting supplies, and then waiting around until they either starved or surrendered. In the meantime, they built towers and assault engines, readying for when the defenders were softened up enough to attack. Anyone for bloodshed?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "*Whistle* This castle really was the jewel in King Richard's crown. He once wrote about Chateau Gaillard: \"How beautiful is my year-old daughter?\" When Philip Augustus had said that he would \"take this castle though its walls were made of iron!\" King Richard retorted that he \"would hold it if its walls were made of butter!\" Then King John the Softsword took over. When Philip was done with this place, you could pour it on your popcorn."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "When Philip Augustus heard about Richard's death in 1199, he set about retaking Normandy. And within three years, in October of 1203, he was knocking on Chateau Gaillard's door with a formidable army. John answered the door with 300 knights, 3,000 horsemen, and 4,000 foot soldiers and assorted ruffians. He tried to surprise Philip's army with a night attack. Big mistake. He wasn't counting on the new cohesion and confidence of Philip's army in the light of Richard's death. They were slaughtered."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, a clever French knight figures out that he and a few men can get into the castle by climbing up through a toilet. So right now, they must be fighting it out at the main gates. By now there'd only be about 60 English soldiers remaining anyway. No wonder this place seems deserted."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These wooden walkways were generally the only way to get around a tower. If a portion of the wall was overrun, they could just remove the walkways and the enemy wouldn't be able to get any further."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These holes in the walls, or they call them arrow loops, were designed to protect archers. while still giving them a wide angle of aim."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These wooden hoardings here, they were put up for defense before a siege to protect archers, and, get this, allow the soldiers to drop big, heavy, painful things on the attackers below. Charming, isn't it?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You want to know what made this castle such a unique piece of military architecture? King Richard's design for the keep and inner bailey. Look, see those rib-like structures ringing the top of the keep? They were designed to funnel drop projectiles down to the skirt-like plinth at the bottom, which bounced the stones in kind of a fan-shaped trajectory. This way there was nowhere that the attackers could approach the castle without being vulnerable."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Ah, the classic garderobe. Simplicity at its finest!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "When an attacker would sap a wall of a castle, they would dig a tunnel underneath the foundation supported by a wooden framework. They would then set fire to the wooden beams and the tunnel would collapse under the wall bringing it down."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGMW_I13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Ah, see that bridge to the inner bailey? This was the castle's one weakness. Under cover of the bridge, Philip Augustus' men managed to dig under the wall. and collapse a section of it in what they called a ... let me look it up ... a \"sapping\" operation."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, Gage, that's the one! That's the one who messed with my sculpture!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That other time traveler must have been doing something over there before you startled him. Maybe that's a good place to start looking."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That chest he was standing over has to have something to do with this."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Maybe the chest is the way into that unmarked room on the plans upstairs."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We're probably going to need a key."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What did that letter say about a secret panel? Maybe that's referring to where they hid the key."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, this must be where the key from the armoire would have worked. Now, if only we could find a duplicate."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's a good thing we went to the trouble of making that key. Now let's see if it works."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's empty! Now why would anyone bother to lock an empty chest? There has to be more to this, Gage, something we've overlooked. I think we should search the rest of the rooms more thoroughly."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm. If what we're looking for isn't in here, maybe it's through here. But how?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, so as far as we know, there's a hidden chamber and a secret panel of some kind. Could there be a hidden panel on or in this chest? What do the doors of the castle under siege have to do with it?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, those plans definitely showed something under this room. I'm willing to bet the family diodes that the way down is through this chest. We just need to find a trigger. And ... do you hear music? Oh, oh well, never mind."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If there were a false bottom to this chest, It might lead down a rickety wooden ladder to a hidden storage chamber full of treasure! Ha, but that kind of thing only happens to Indie!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I wonder what that letter meant by, \"dores of the assaged castel.\" Surely they wouldn't hide the treasure by the front doors. Maybe they were referring to something else?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H14
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "There's that tapestry of a besieged castle. I wonder if King John was referring to that!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_H15
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If you push on the doors in the tapestry, maybe it will trigger something."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It looks like the supplies are pretty depleted."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGSR_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wow, will you look at those kegs? Probably not much left in them this far in the siege. What I'm trying to figure out is where do you put the tap?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTR_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "There's no way that jewel was made by medieval hands. It's refracting light from your helmet in an almost perfectly mathematical pattern. It's flawless. I don't know what it is, but it definitely does not belong on that sword."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTR_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, we're obviously in the right place. Now we just need to pinpoint what's been changed."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTR_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think this would be a good time to use your locate biochip. I don't think we have time to cross-reference every object in this room."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTR_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's an enamel on leather portrait of Richard and John's grandfather, Geoffrey Plantagenet, made in 1158. Nice likeness, huh? It's one of the few pieces still around in my time. Too bad if you chip away the enamel and gold leaf, you can still see the numbers. Since life was so difficult in the Middle Ages, what with constant wars, and plagues and whatnot, people just didn't have time for art. The knowledge of the masters of past generations wasn't passed on and was eventually forgotten. That's why everything from this period of history was pretty crude compared to the ages before and after it. And very little of it has survived because it was mostly in the form of tapestries. and book illuminations, most of which have perished."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTSVID1
#. Speaker: English Knight
msgid "Norman traitor! You shall not flee now!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTS_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We must adhere to the Prime Directive, Spock. Non--interference."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTS_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Call it a hunch, but I don't think we're getting in."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTS_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I've got a nagging suspicion that the room on the other side of this door was neither modeled nor rendered. What the hell does that mean?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTS_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Sounds locked to me."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTS_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's kind of interesting how they use the more finished stone on the outside of the walls. to make the castle look more imposing and use the rough stone on the inside. The space in between was generally filled with rubble and, oh, I don't know, annoying singing frogs in metal boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTTVID1
#. Speaker: English Knight
msgid "Haro!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If someone should get a glimpse of us up here, in this suit, we might pass as a knight, but I think we should be careful not to be seen."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, looks like the only way out of here is down."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It doesn't look like he's going to need that arrow anymore."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think you should take the arrow."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The wooden roofs were covered with tin, I think to prevent being set ablaze by flaming arrows."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Those boulders were dropped on any nimrod trying to climb the walls."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Château Gaillard, France (1204 AD)
#. Track ID: CGTT_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That big wooden thing over there is a siege tower. Philip Augustus terrorized the defenders by surrounding the castle with fourteen of these. They're pretty handy for being able to shoot over the wall of a castle, but they did have one minor drawback. Can you say \"flammable\"?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I recognize these sketches. This is the Codex Atlanticus. It is his most famous manuscript, covering some of his most prolific studies."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, that's nice. Serves you right for buying Mail-Order. It'll translate every known language, but it can't recognize Latin written backwards? And you didn't even get a set of Ginsu knives."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, what was that flash of light?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "He's not in here. That flash of light must have been him jumping out when he saw you on the balcony. He must have startled him."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hope we didn't forget anything."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_C08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Mom."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Whoa! Did you forget to set the emergency brake? Let's just hope we can get through that door."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We're either going to have to use a key or resort to a little breaking and entering."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Maybe that key you got from the other tower would work in this door."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, unless you want to go looking for a key, I'd suggest using something from our inventory to pry the door open."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Whatever's been altered has got to be in this room. I'd suggest using your evidence biochip."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If the other agent's suit is the same as yours, then in order to drop that lens filter, he must have had it out of his temporal pocket, which means that he was using it. If that's the case, then maybe it can help you find whatever it is he changed."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Try looking around a bit while you've got that lens filter on."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What is that? Not something from this time, that's for sure. The other agent must have dropped it by accident. I wouldn't leave it there, it'll probably cause a temporal distortion."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "They look pretty normal, but who knows? It could be something hidden here that we just can't see."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If there was a secret message in the writings, someone would have found it, unless it was invisible to most forms of detection."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, I've got it. Try using that lens filter you picked up."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_H12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "What do you want to know? It's a human heart. If you're that spellbound by it, take it with you. I'm sure Leonardo has spares."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's locked! Talk about paranoid. Just look what we had to go through just to get up here."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Leonardo's private study! I'd imagine very few people have even seen this."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, da Vinci's drum machine. Who'd have thought that Leonardo would have been the spiritual ancestor of the Pet Shop Boys? Actually, though, da Vinci was also an accomplished musician and composer, and designed several musical instruments, such as the viola organista."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, these are da Vinci's notebooks! Or, three of them anyway."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "More flying machines. Da Vinci began studying flight here in Milan, and it remained an obsession for him until the last years of his life. He actually made some remarkably keen observations on air resistance, the eddying motion of fluids, and the mechanics of the flight of birds. It's even been said that he himself attempted to fly, but that's really just a legend."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Cool, but where are the action figures to go with them? Probably back at your place, eh, Gage? Sorry. Now, those aren't toys, so be careful."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, preserves. A human heart. Looks like we're on Hannibal Lecter's pantry. \"I ate his liver with a flying machine and a nice Chianti.\""
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's no wonder Leonardo was being so secretive, human dissection was strictly prohibited by The Church. and might have gotten him arrested if anyone were to find out about it. Certainly the scandal wouldn't have put him in the Duke's favor. The elevator seems like it would have been a good idea for getting the cadavers up here on the quiet, though."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, look at these sketches. Da Vinci originally began studying anatomy as a foundation for his art, but his insatiable thirst for knowledge eventually drew him to the study of the human body in a lot more depth. In one of his writings, he talks of 120 books of anatomy that he had written. None of them were ever found, but what notes and sketches have survived. show that he did an in-depth study of human physiology. No one else had mapped the human body as comprehensively, partly due to the interdiction from The Church."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCT_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think it's jammed. Whoever was up here before us wasn't particularly careful."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I quote da Vinci, translated from the original Latin: \"Weebles wobble, but they don't fall down.\""
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "With all of these these siege machines laying around, there's got to be something out here that'll help us get into that tower."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I wonder if there might be some way to get in from outside the tower. If we could just get up to that balcony."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wow, this looks like a ballista, but it's huge! Judging from the amount of rope there, it's probably meant to be shot at something pretty far away. I wonder if it's used for naval combat or something."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, since the room at the top of the tower is wider than the rest of the tower, it's impossible to hook it with a grappling hook from directly below. But from here, we've got a pretty good angle on it. The only problem is that we're too far away. But I'd be willing to bet that this ballista could cover the distance."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Of course, I have no idea how you'd climb all the way up to the balcony in this suit, especially without a wall or something for leverage."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, this must be what shoots the grappling hook for that climbing cycle contraption."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I think we may be in luck. From here we've got a pretty good angle on the tower."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Climb up there and see if you can hook the balcony."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That crank there looks like it's for gross positioning. You'll probably need to aim the ballista in the general direction you want to shoot before getting on."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, there's a lever and two cranks. The lever's obviously for firing the grappling hook. The cranks must control the direction and angle of aim. It looks like the direction crank is only for making minor adjustments to aim, so you may have to get off. and find a way to make it point in the general direction first."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H14
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Okay, we're almost there. There's no way you're going to be able to hand-over-hand that far wearing your jumpsuit. Not without a wall or something for leverage. If we could just find some other way to climb this rope, we'd be set."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H15
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, we're halfway there. We've got the rope leading up to the tower. Now, all we need is the cycle."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H16
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Why are you standing around asking questions? Hook the cycle onto the rope and get us up there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_H17
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, I think I just figured out what that cycle thing is for. Try hanging it from the rope."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, there's no question what kept da Vinci the busiest. With his patron waging war against the Venetians, there must have been a lot of pressure on him to give the Duke a strategic advantage."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, a primitive harvester! A harvester of human lives! *Cackling*. Sorry, too many episodes of Tales from the Crypt. Still, those chopped hay bales are ... *grunt* ... making me a little queasy."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So that's how he keeps his hedges so well-groomed."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, clever. Now, if they were inflatable, then you'd have something."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh, you don't want to go over there. That's where Presto put all the cheap low-res models."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Look, if they let us go everywhere, they never would have finished the game."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I've seen this in da Vinci's sketchbooks. It's cleverly designed to hit the operator in the head with a barrage of rocks."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Da Vinci designed a series of these multi-barreled guns. predating the invention of the Gatling gun by close to 400 years."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Ah, yes. An interesting perspective, but uh, I'm getting a little nervous, okay?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's a large mortar."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I14
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It looks like da Vinci was testing out some of his designs for siege defenses as well. Trying to outwit himself, I guess. I wonder who's winning."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSCY_I15
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Yep, straddling this baby's got to really make you feel like a man."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wow, a-mazing. With all the different things da Vinci had his hands in, he still had time to keep this place looking pretty."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Maybe this won't be as easy as I thought, Gage. It looks like we're going to have to find another way up to the tower room."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, we have access to all of da Vinci's workshop. There's got to be something we can use to get up into that tower."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Now, da Vinci's main purpose here was to design war machines for the Duke. I'm sure he must have devised something for scaling castle walls."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's a pretty ingenious device. There must be a system of cogwheels driven by that turnstile that run in that triple helix track. Kind of neat for moving furniture, but I'll take the stairs any day."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSGD_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Notice there isn't a pulley system down here to lower the platform? I'm sure that was by design. Da Vinci was known to be very secretive, even paranoid, and he liked his privacy."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm. Maybe we should try and get our bearings before we start searching around."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Let's take a look outside and see what's around."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, no staircase. There's a pulley system across from us with a rope going down it. Looks like a cog track ringing the outside. It might be some kind of dumbwaiter."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, if it's an elevator, we should be able to bring it back up. Maybe we should try using the pulley to bring up whatever's down there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Try the mechanism across from us."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Pretty heavy duty. There's a rope that goes down through the floor, probably to a counterweight. The controls look pretty straightforward, though."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It's probably really simple to operate. One of those levers must be a brake. It would help if we could read the labels. Can you translate Latin?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "You're not one of those people who doesn't like to read directions, are you? Just translate the labels, find out how to unlock the thing, and wheel it up."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, guessing from the direction of the tracks, I think we would need to push the turnstile counterclockwise to go down."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Um, correct me if I'm wrong, but you can't be here twice at the same time, can you? So if that's not you, there's another agent messing around over there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_H11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Well, I don't think we have to look any further. This is going to be easy. Whatever was tampered with is going to be in that other tower. We *might* even be able to catch him in the act."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, is this real? Are we really in Leonardo's studio?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is Leonardo's Portrait of a Musician. This is supposed to be a friend of his, Atlante Migliorotti, whom he traveled to Milan with, but historians were never sure. I suppose if we waited until morning we could find out for certain, but, well, I guess we could save that for the next trip."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I wonder if Leonardo realizes he'll never finish this piece. If records are correct, he's been working on it for - what, are we in 1488? - about three years now, with another two to go before he gives up on it for some reason. I wonder why. They have some falling out? You know, we could jump a couple of years forward and- Okay. Sorry. Wrong time."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "These two pieces were actually done a lot earlier when Leonardo was in his 20s and in Verrocchio's workshop. You can tell he probably had a gargantuan ego by then."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Now, the one on the ground is an interesting example of da Vinci's sense of humor. It's a portrait of Ginevra de' Benci, the sister of a friend of Leonardo. She was ill and suffering from heartache from a tragically ended affair, apparently a serious illness at the time. The plant behind her, though, is a juniper, which in old Italian is ginevro, so it's actually a pun on her name."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is one of two versions of the Virgin of the Rocks that Leonardo painted. This one was commissioned by a monastery. This really would have made da Vinci's name in Milan. They'd never seen anything like it before."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The subject of this painting is Cecilia Gallerani, one of the Duke's favorite mistresses. The animal she's holding is an ermine, which in Greek is called \"gale\". Leonardo really had an obsession with symbolism. It didn't take much to keep him amused."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Beatrice D'Este, the Duke of Milan's wife. This was painted to commemorate their wedding. I wonder what he has it back up in his studio for."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I hope this wasn't a tryout as parachute designs."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "This is one of a whole series of sketches that Leonardo did for a massive 24-foot sculpture that he was planning. It was to be of the Duke's father, Francesco Sforza, on horseback. It was one of the works he had originally proposed in order to get the job here in the first place. But, like a lot of things he designed, he never got around to actually making it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "I don't know if I want to try that thing. Da Vinci had a lot of ideas that were ahead of their time, but, frankly, most of them wouldn't have worked. And I don't know if I want to die ahead of my time."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Da Vinci really was a master of contraptions. It looks like when the Duke of Milan allowed him to build this place, he got a chance to field test a lot of his ideas."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Gage, you really have to be careful not to leave a mark on history. That could be a temporal ripple right there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I14
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That must be Milan in the distance."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSPT_I15
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wow, old il Moro must have been pretty impressed by Leonardo's letter of introduction to fund this. This is amazing!"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_C01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hmm, interesting. Are you thinking what I'm thinking?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "If there are drawings of this thing lying here, da Vinci must have been planning on building it."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "So, this is what that device in the plans is for. It looked like there were parts near them, too."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Ahhhh, these must be the plans for that rope-climbing bike thing. Wonder if he's made one of these yet?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Some of those parts I saw laying around look like the ones in this drawing. If we can't find one of these things that's already been completed, maybe we can make one."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Judging from the drawing, you'll need the three complete assemblies and pegs to hold it together."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Hey, this looks familiar. Now, if only we had wheels and gears and a rocket scientist to put it together...! I'm starting to get an idea of what it feels like to be a parent on Christmas Eve. I don't suppose we could go wake up Leonardo, could we?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "All right, we can build this thing. All we have to do is gather the parts we need and then just follow the plans."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "We can put it together right here on the jig. Just connect the other parts to the one that's already there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Looks like he's still working the snags out of that wheelbarrow invention. Oh, no, I know what this is! It's part of the climbing machine! I recognize it from the drawing."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oh yeah, that's definitely part of the climbing cycle on the drawing. Unless Leonardo was also working on a moped."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Locked!? Oh, you've got to be kidding me! Well, if they're so anal as to lock up their tools every night, something tells me they wouldn't leave a key lying around. So, we better start looking elsewhere unless you want to risk a temporal distortion by busting this thing open."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_H12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "According to the plans, we first have to put the three assemblies together, then hammer the pegs in to hold- Hammer the pegs in... uh... We do have pegs *and* a hammer, don't we?"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "It looks like da Vinci actually got a chance to put into practice his ideas for constructing a large dome. As a matter of fact, I believe this was the year that he entered a competition to design. the cupola for the unfinished cathedral of Milan. Unfortunately, the much larger dome of the cathedral was a bigger architectural challenge, which may have been why he mysteriously withdrew from the contest. It was in fact, Leonardo's rival, Brunelleschi of Florence, who eventually solved the problem."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I02
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The architecture of this studio seems to incorporate a lot of ideas that Leonardo explores in his sketchbooks. He also seems very influenced by Florentine architecture of the period."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I03
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Da Vinci was really ahead of his time in his conception of flying machines. Though none of his designs would actually have left the ground, he did presage the invention of helicopters and parachutes."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I04
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The machine with the wings is an early design for an ornithopter, an attempt at flying by imitating the mechanics of birds. The pilot's pedaling would make the wings flap through a linkage of cords and pulleys, theoretically letting you fly like a bird. Of course, the whole design is too heavy to get itself off the ground, let alone the 300-pound body builder you'd need to pedal it anywhere near fast enough."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I05
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Lodovico Sforza, il Moro, the current Duke of Bari, is actually a usurper. His young nephew, Gian Galeazzo, is the rightful heir, but hey, what are uncles for!? \"Let me handle things till you grow up, kid!\" Pity he never got the chance. No big surprise that the kid died mysteriously before assuming the head of the family. The court of Milan was renowned for its pageantry, art, and music. Leonardo's previous patron, Lorenzo di Medici, may have sent him here. knowing that the gesture would placate his powerful and ambitious neighbor. Though why da Vinci made the move has always been a mystery. All this, of course, would seem to be a strong motivation."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I06
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Still under construction. With the current war against the Venetian Republic, money must have been coming in sporadically."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I07
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Looks like school's in. Always good to keep a bunch of students and apprentices handy. to boost your standing and do all the grunt work for you. Like most Renaissance artists, Da Vinci believed that designing and giving orders were gentleman's work, and actually executing the piece was work for servants. That's why he rarely finished anything. Okay, okay. A little professional jealousy."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I08
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That hoist design looks like the one that Leonardo sketched up for the casting. of the horse sculpture he was planning, but never got around to. Well, at least you got use out of the hoist."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I09
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Wow, he actually tried to make the tank. Looks like he succeeded. I'd like to see the six burly guys who are going to make this thing move at any kind of speed, though. The guys inside would be well protected, but when you attack someone in a UFO, you can pretty much kiss the element of surprise goodbye."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I10
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "My god, Renaissance power tools. Da Vinci was the 15th-century Bob Vila."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I11
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "He's invented the table saw? Now this is stretching my suspension of disbelief. \"Hand crank to get the flywheel up to speed, and in minutes you have an attractive new den!\""
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I12
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "That's an interesting gear assembly. It's geared pretty low. I wonder what it's for."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I13
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Typical. You can't read the instructions just like those Japanese model kits."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I14
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Oohh, here are sketches of the elevator we took. It would have helped if these were at the top. He makes it look so simple, doesn't he? Okay, maybe not."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I15
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "He didn't really mean for you to ride that thing naked, did he? You could get something caught in there."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Leonardo da Vinci's Studio, Italy (1488 AD)
#. Track ID: DSWS_I16
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "The big screw-shaped device is conceptually pretty close to a helicopter. If it were light and powerful enough, it might just get you off the ground. Just enough for you to start spinning in the other direction without anything like a tail rotor stabilizing you. Still, that's an example of the amazing flexibility of da Vinci's mind."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Farnstein's Lab (2247 AD) or Gage's Apartment (2318 AD)
#. Track ID: FAERVID3
#. Speaker: Geno Andrews
msgid "Hi, I'm not here right now. At a rehearsal, you know the routine. Uh, name, number, I'll get back to you. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Farnstein's Lab (2247 AD) or Gage's Apartment (2318 AD)
#. Track ID: FAERVID3
#. Speaker: Woman
msgid "Hi it's me. I know it's been a while but ... I found some things that belong to you. If you like, you can stop by and pick them up sometime. I'll be home this evening. It's just some records and papers and pictures, but, you know, I thought you might like to have them. Okay, bye bye."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Farnstein's Lab (2247 AD) or Gage's Apartment (2318 AD)
#. Track ID: FAERVID3
#. Speaker: Geno Andrews
msgid "~ You were like the wind moving fast and silent ~. ~ Never knowing where you were going, or where you'd been ~. ~ I pray somehow you hear these vows I've thrown into the wind ~. ~ And while you're gone, I'm moving on. I'll begin again ~. ~ Right or wrong, you're wondering if I'll be standing strong. You have my word ~. ~ I promise I'll be searching for a reason to go on ~"
msgstr ""

#. Location: Farnstein's Lab (2247 AD) or Gage's Apartment (2318 AD)
#. Track ID: FAERVID5
#. Speaker: Michelle (Agent 3)
msgid "Okay. This cartridge is the final piece you'll need to build a time machine. You should also have the Da Vinci codex, which contains various formulae, the sculpture which morphs into a schematic diagram, and the medieval sword which holds the energy focusing element. This cartridge contains all existing notes, plans, and diagrams on the construction of. the neutrino matrix accelerator, the time machine's power source. You'll be able to recreate the accelerator from these notes. By using the formulae, schematics, and focusing element to control the accelerator. and harness its power, you'll be able to turn it into a functioning time machine. The information on this cartridge has been arranged in chronological order, starting with the building of the accelerator's framework, and following the process of its construction to the final pieces. Good luck- Sorry to interrupt, Gage, but I need that back."
msgstr ""

#. Location: Farnstein's Lab (2247 AD) or Gage's Apartment (2318 AD)
#. Track ID: FAER_I01
#. Speaker: Arthur
msgid "Yes, it's Lava Lamp 2328."
msgstr ""

